cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the data it produces in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "astro-forecast: A high-precision astronomical forecasting and calendar factual archive"
abstract: >-
  An open-source toolchain that separates astronomical computation from page
  rendering, built for publishing traditional Chinese calendrical and
  astronomical content on WordPress over the long term. The compute kernel is
  based on Skyfield and the JPL DE421 ephemeris and derives solar-term instants,
  eclipses, planetary conjunctions/oppositions/stationary points, greatest
  elongations, lunar phase and age, meteor-shower maxima, and sunrise/sunset with
  twilight. All values are computed offline and delivered to a WordPress site in
  batches over a REST endpoint; the front end performs no live computation. The
  plugin ships eight shortcodes and eight templates covering today's sky, upcoming
  events, this day in history, observing locations, and report download.
  Code is MIT-licensed; data and documentation inside the repository
  (samples/, data/, docs/, README*.md) are CC BY 4.0. The ephemeris file
  de421.bsp is not redistributed here; its rights belong to JPL / NASA.
